    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--sleep-on-idle` and `--language-only` (encoder transfer backend `zmq_to_scheduler` or `mooncake`), every multimodal request takes about 1 s longer than it should, however small the image.\n\nWhen the request reaches the scheduler, it waits in `mm_receiver.waiting_list` for its embeddings. Nothing else is runnable, so the event loop calls `maybe_sleep_on_idle()`, which blocks in `IdleSleeper.maybe_sleep()` → `poller.poll(1000)`. That poller only watches `recv_from_tokenizer` and `recv_from_rpc`. The embeddings arrive on the request's own receive socket, which the poller doesn't see, so the request is only picked up when the 1 s poll times out.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `Scheduler.maybe_sleep_on_idle`: don't sleep while `mm_receiver` has waiting requests. The loop keeps polling the receive sockets until the embeddings land, then sleeps normally once nothing is waiting. Nothing changes when EPD is off (`mm_receiver is None`) or when no request is waiting.\n- New CPU unit test `test/registered/unit/managers/test_idle_sleep_epd_wait.py` (`base-a-test-cpu`). It covers the pending-embedding case, which fails on the current code and passes with this change, plus both cases where sleeping must still happen.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A: scheduling only, no change to model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nQwen4Exp language server on one GPU with `--sleep-on-idle --language-only`, plus an `--encoder-only` server on a second GPU. Each request is one image plus a short prompt, about 15 output tokens, end to end. The 512×512 row uses a new image each time; the other rows are the second request for the same image:\n\n| Image | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| 512×512 | 1.19 s | 0.19 s |\n| 1024×1024 | 1.17 s | 0.30 s |\n| 1920×1080 | 1.17 s | 0.53 s |\n\n(The encoder took 26 ms to encode the 512×512 image. Before the fix, the scheduler log showed prefill starting about 1 s after `/encode completed`, with a 6 ms `queue_duration`.)\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). (ruff 0.15.1 format/check and isort 7.0.0 on the changed files)\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (N/A)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39433230322](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39433230322)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39433230316](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39433230316)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39433230220](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39433230220)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
